        "data": {
          "title": "Old Trail Museum – Rocky Mountain Front Interpretive Center",
          "summary": "The Old Trail Museum is building a new multi-purpose facility to house the Rocky Mountain Front Interpretive Center, a multidisciplinary space developed with MT FWP, scientists, and outdoor recreation experts to exhibit the natural history, ecology, and diverse wildlife of the Rocky Mountain Front.",
          "intro": "The Old Trail Museum is constructing a new multi-purpose building to house the Rocky Mountain Front Interpretive Center, a multidisciplinary interpretive space developed in collaboration with Montana Fish, Wildlife & Parks, scientists, experts, and outdoor recreationalists. The center will exhibit the unique natural history, ecology, and diverse wildlife of the Rocky Mountain Front, and will serve as a visitor center hub, event center, and community meeting space for educational programming and lecture series.",
